TI  - Developing an Assurance Case for an Optical Communication Mission in a Model Based Setting
T2  - 2022 68TH ANNUAL RELIABILITY AND MAINTAINABILITY SYMPOSIUM (RAMS 2022)
CP  - 68th Annual Reliability and Maintainability Symposium (RAMS)
AB  - NASA's Office of Safety and Mission Assurance has adopted an objectives-based approach to standards to ensure that the Safety and Mission Assurance disciplines and programs are addressing the challenges of NASA's changing missions, acquisition and engineering practices, and technology. Starting with the Reliability and Maintainability discipline, an objectives hierarchy was developed to systematically decompose technical considerations that form the basis for that discipline.
   This paper shows how the objectives-based approach can be applied to SETH+, a mission concept with a novel aspect - demonstration of optical communication from a smallsat spacecraft to Earth across a distance of 0.1 AU (Astronomical Unit) - approximately 15,000,000 km. The objectives hierarchy supports development of an assurance case, done in a manner that draws upon Model Based Systems Engineering's representations of model information.
