TI  - MBSE Challenges in the Concurrent Preliminary Design of CubeSats: Nanospace Study
T2  - SYSCON 2022: THE 16TH ANNUAL IEEE INTERNATIONAL SYSTEMS CONFERENCE (SYSCON)
CP  - 16th Annual IEEE International Systems Conference (SysCon)
AB  - In this paper, the early endeavours of the incorporation of a Model-based Systems Engineering (MBSE) approach to the open-source Nanospace framework is discussed, presenting the challenges that need to be overcome for such an integration. Nanospace is a web application dedicated to facilitate concurrent engineering during the preliminary design phase of CubeSats.
   CubeSats provide a progression of educational and research opportunities, and have had increased the accessibility to space for non-space fairing nations. CubeSats and their subsystems interfaces have been studied numerous times. Nanospace may benefit from MBSE, as MBSE facilitates knowledge reuse; which could allow a faster design convergence and faster inspection of candidate architectures.
