T2  - 2025 IEEE INTERNATIONAL GEOSCIENCE AND REMOTE SENSING SYMPOSIUM (IGARSS)
CP  - 2025 International Geoscience and Remote Sensing Symposium-IGARSS-Annual
AB  - Capella Space is working towards SAR interferometry. This contribution provides an overview of recent advances, focusing on orbital tube requirement to achieve repeat-ground-track orbits, orbital selection and interferometric examples. An experimental active orbit control algorithm has been applied to Capella-14 and Capella-13 satellites, at 45 degree and 53 degree inclination, respectively. The requirement for the orbital tube was set to 250 m radius, and the repeat cycle 2.95 days.
